OL,3,GNEWSABreastfeeding may leave lasting
OL,4,Aimprint on genes
OL,5,
OL,6,FBreastfeeding may leave a lasting
OL,7,Fbiological imprint on babies,
OL,8,Fscientists say, in findings welcomed by
OL,9,Fmothers.
OL,11,FResearchers from the University of
OL,12,FExeter, in Devon, identified traces in
OL,13,Fthe blood of children who were
OL,14,Fexclusively breastfed that remained
OL,15,Fdetectable years later in a global
OL,16,Fstudy involving thousands of children.
OL,18,FThe traces are linked to epigenetic
OL,19,Fchanges, which affect how genes behave
OL,20,Fwithout altering the genes themselves.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,346,340,200,160,0,100
